<BaseLayout title="Research | Prateek Gupta">

<SectionTitle title="Research" eyebrow="Topological ML · Phenotyping" />

<p style="font-size:0.95rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:20px;">
  My research interests span Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Intelligent Systems, Cybersecurity, Time Series Modeling, and mathematical learning frameworks for structured and multimodal data. My recent work includes Persistent Homology for plant phenotyping, semantic federated intrusion detection, spatiotemporal sensor fault recovery, and early crisis detection using latent dynamical systems and multimodal instability analysis.
</p>


<PublicationItem
  title="Topological Analysis of Plant Structure Using PH for Genotype Classification"
  venue="ACM ICVGIP"
  year="2025"
  desc="Implemented full PH pipeline: segmentation, skeletonization, filtrations, persistence images, and classification (RF, SVM, MLP). Achieved 94% accuracy."
  pdfLink="/cv/plant_ph_paper.pdf"
/>
<PublicationItem
  title="COSINE: Federated Semantic Intrusion Detection with Calibrated Gated Rejection"
  venue="Accepted at IEEE ICSCCC 2026, NIT Jalandhar"
  year="2026"
  desc="Proposed a semantic, open-set federated intrusion detection framework using LLM-grounded attack semantics and similarity-based gated rejection. Achieved 97.8% robust accuracy with 92%+ coverage on NSL-KDD under non-IID federated settings."
  pdfLink="public/cv/COSINE.pdf"
/>

<PublicationItem
  title="Belief-Aware Spatiotemporal Fault Detection and Recovery in Environmental Sensor Networks"
  venue="Under Review at Reliability Engineering & System Safety"
  year="2026"
  desc="Proposed a belief-aware spatiotemporal framework for robust fault detection, recovery, and sensor reliability inference. Developed a recovery-aware fusion mechanism to stabilize post-fault transitions and suppress reconstruction oscillations. Achieved ROC-AUC of 0.977 with over 70% reconstruction error reduction."
/>

<PublicationItem
  title="Latent Information Instability Framework for Early Crisis Detection"
  venue="Under Review at IEEE Transactions on Computational Social Systems"
  year="2026"
  desc="Developed a latent dynamical framework for robust early crisis detection using multimodal instability signals. Modeled crisis evolution using Hidden Markov Models to capture latent transitions across evolving crisis phases. Achieved 0.86 early detection rate on real-world disaster benchmark datasets."
/>


